tt has raised far more money directly, but Democratic outside groups have spent heavily against him, and headlines show attacks on his healthcare record alongside his effort to distance himself from Trump on foreign policy. The race has drawn heavy attention, including televised debates and a toss-up rating from MLive.\n\nExpert raters split between toss-up and lean Democratic with a flip, and prediction markets give Lawrence roughly a 56 to 75 percent chance. The lone recent poll shows a narrow Democratic lead, though it is weeks old and from a Democratic-leaning sponsor. The overall picture is a close race tilting modestly to Democrats, with meaningful uncertainty in both directions.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6879, "margin": 2.86}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6475, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7011, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6783, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6189, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6168, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6888, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7095, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.6925, "margin": 3.0}]}